<title>FRANCE: Castorama to buy 90.2 pct of Reno Depot.</title>
<headline>Castorama to buy 90.2 pct of Reno Depot.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French furniture retailer Castorama said on Monday it has offered to buy 90.2 percent of the capital of Reno-Depot Inc, a leading retailer of home improvement products in Quebec.</p>
<p>Reno-Depot had 1996 turnover of C$431.5 million, the French company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The buy out is conditional on U.S. Home Depot Inc not exercising a pre-emptive right on the capital of Reno-Depot. If Castorama's offer is accepted, it will bid for the 9.8 percent of Reno in public hands.</p>
<p>No price details were given.</p>
<p>(( -- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 ))</p>
</text>
